// Grounded Brain: GenAI Core Architecture (Streamlined Pipeline)
// Eraser "Flow Chart" diagram-as-code. Paste into a new Flow Chart at https://app.eraser.io
title GenAI Core: OpenAI · Mem0 · Vector DB (Pinecone / Qdrant)
direction right
colorMode bold

// ----- Stage 1: Client & Input -----
User [shape: oval, icon: user, color: gray, label: "User / Client\n(Uploads docs · Asks questions)"]

// ----- Stage 2: Orchestration -----
Express API [icon: nodejs, color: green, label: "Express API\nRAG Orchestration & Prompt Assembly"]
Inngest [icon: zap, color: purple, label: "Inngest Workers\nBackground Processing & Sync"]

// ----- Stage 3: Context & Memory Engines -----
VectorDB [icon: database, color: blue, label: "Pinecone / Qdrant\nVector Database\nWHY: Top-K semantic chunk search\nWorkspace-isolated retrieval"]
Mem0 [icon: brain, color: purple, label: "Mem0\nLong-Term Memory Layer\nWHY: User preferences across chats\nContinuous fact learning"]

// ----- Stage 4: AI Intelligence -----
OpenAI [icon: openai, color: orange, label: "OpenAI Engine\nLLM & Embeddings\nWHY: text-embedding-3-small (1536d)\ngpt-4o-mini / gpt-4o generation"]

// ----- Stage 5: Output -----
Reply [shape: oval, icon: message-circle, color: green, label: "Streamed Reply\nGrounded answer with citations [1]"]

// ----- Clean Forward Traversal (Left to Right) -----
// Ingestion Flow
User > Inngest: 1. Upload source (PDF, Web, Video)
Inngest > OpenAI: Embed text chunks (1536d)
Inngest > VectorDB: Store vectors & chunk metadata

// Chat RAG Flow
User > Express API: 2. Ask question in workspace
Express API > VectorDB: Search relevant chunks
VectorDB > OpenAI: Top-K passages with page numbers
Express API > Mem0: Fetch user preferences
Mem0 > OpenAI: Relevant user facts
Express API > OpenAI: Assemble grounded prompt
OpenAI > Reply: Streamed response with citations [1]

// Continuous Learning Flow
Inngest > Mem0: 3. Learn new user facts from chat turns
